Package: amber-fonts
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Hyperquader <hyperquader@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: fontconfig
Section: fonts
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/Hyperquader-Coders/amber-fonts
Description: SauceCodePro Nerd Font for the Amber Linux suite
 The typeface every Amber Linux application draws with, packaged once so
 that copal, kat800 and amberlin depend on it instead of each carrying
 their own copy of the same files.
 .
 Two families are shipped and they are not interchangeable. "SauceCodePro
 Nerd Font" draws its icons at their natural width, which is what Copal
 and Amberlin want because they draw notes rather than a grid.
 "SauceCodePro Nerd Font Mono" squeezes each icon into exactly one
 character cell, which is what kat800 needs because VTE is a character
 grid. Both are monospaced for text — the difference is the icons.
 .
 The faces are Source Code Pro (Adobe) patched with additional glyphs by
 the Nerd Fonts project, both under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. No
 Debian package carries the Nerd Fonts patch, which is why the suite
 ships it itself: a missing family is a silent fallback to whatever Pango
 picks, which is invisible in the code and obvious on screen.
